{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^def |''^    def |''^class '\"' paid_gate.py; nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '143,211p'; tail -18 rehearsal.log; tail -10 paid-mutants.log\"","aggregated_output":"45:def W(population, measure, scope, period):\n49:def bands(draw, view_id):\n55:def passages(draw, evidence_ids):\n63:def pair_family(draw, total, dc):\n71:def only(family, view_id):\n75:def questions(draw, view_ids):\n85:def shown_lines(user):\n95:def item(unit, arm, draw, calls, family, shown):\n103:def build_plan():\n117:def plan(out):\n136:def strip(data):\n140:class Gate:\n141:    def __init__(self, out, transport, ledger=None):\n147:    def request(self, it, user):\n150:    def record(self, line):\n154:    def attempt(self, it, draw, user, n):\n181:    def unit(self, it, draw):\n190:    def run(self, items):\n202:def attempt_records(out, damaged=None):\n216:def derive_finals(out, items, damaged=None):\n245:def summarise(out, items, ledger_state):\n266:def _same_value(a, b):\n273:def merge(parts, shared_keys):\n343:def recover(out):\n352:def budget_module():\n360:def send(out, approved, plan_path):\n401:def normalise(calc, prefix=''):\n427:def run_digest(out):\n435:def card_view(calc, view_id, recorded, prefix=''):\n462:def packet_units(results, items):\n477:def card_lines(base, fam, v, token, data, final_label, prefix=''):\n499:def packet_body(items, unit, arm, decision, per_card):\n522:def key_commitment(key):\n526:def render_packets(out, key):\n542:def render_attempts(out, labels):\n559:def packets(out, key_dir):\n584:def _grounded(ground, grounds):\n589:def final_readings(pid, cards, members, grounds=()):\n612:def verdict(out, readings_path, key_dir):\n   143\t    - one was stale, because packets now render from the attempts;\n   144\t    - one was masked by the shared-only filter, and a shared within-call case was added;\n   145\t    - one disabled only half a condition.\n   146\t  - One mutant is equivalent and is left out: unifying any key across calls, not only declared shared ones. C3 looks only at\n   147\t    forecasts reachable from each member's own outcome, so the result does not change.\n   148\t\n   149\t## 3e. After council round 47d (`codex-r47d.md`): three structural rules\n   150\t\n   151\tRounds 47b to 47d kept finding the same two things: process information inside the readers' packets, and a mapping from packets to\n   152\tunits that could change after reading. These findings were answered by rule, not one by one.\n   153\t\n   154\t1. **The scoring text holds only what the four questions need.** For each card: the question, the ladder, the passages it names,\n   155\t   its own figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. It carries no attempt history, no code decision\n   156\t   and no check code. The verdict applies the code's decision itself.\n   157\t   - Earlier attempts go to `attempts.md`. That file is for diagnostic reading only and is never scored. Each attempt sits under its\n   158\t     own shuffled label (D01, …), with no link to a packet. [47d.3]\n   159\t   - A card with no final answer says why in plain words: no request was sent; the request was started and no answer was recorded;\n   160\t     no answer arrived; the answer was refused and its retry was not sent; or the answer did not match the format. [47d.4]\n   161\t2. **The text the readers receive commits to the mapping.** The key is {a random salt, the run's digest, the packet order, the\n   162\t   attempt labels}. Its sha256 is the first line of `packets.md`. The verdict refuses a key whose sha256 differs from that line. It\n   163\t   also renders the packets again from the run and the key, and refuses a mismatch with `packets.md` or with the readings' sha256.\n   164\t   A swap of two packets with identical text is caught, and so is a decision written into the key. [47d.1]\n   165\t3. **Reconciliation is one to one.** A declared shared forecast is unified only when each of the two calls holds exactly one\n   166\t   candidate for that quantity and scenario, and their values are the same. Otherwise every copy stays, for C3 and C4 to judge as in a\n   167\t   joint answer. [47d.2]\n   168\t\n   169\t- **The record:** an attempt that was started and not finished is kept in `results.json` as interrupted.\n   170\t- **Rehearsal:** 51 of 51, three times (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n   171\t  - the scoring text has no attempt, decision or code;\n   172\t  - the refused first answer appears only in `attempts.md`;\n   173\t  - a swap of identical-text packets is INCOMPLETE;\n   174\t  - a forged key is INCOMPLETE;\n   175\t  - two equal shared forecasts in the second call are refused (C4, three nodes);\n   176\t  - an interrupted card says the request was started.\n   177\t- **Mutants:** 20 of 20 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   178\t\n   179\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   180\t\n   181\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   182\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   183\t  - Each packet shows, per card (K1, K2), the question, the ladder, every passage the final answer names (as the request showed it),\n   184\t    its figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. Nothing about attempts or the code's decision is\n   185\t    shown (§3e).\n   186\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. The verdict, not the reader, applies the code's\n   187\t    decision: its cards cannot count as usable.\n   188\t  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n   189\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   190\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   191\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   192\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   193\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   194\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   195\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   196\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   197\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines):\n   198\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   199\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   200\t    singleton answers.\n   201\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   202\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n   203\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n   204\t\n   205\t## 5. What the result decides\n   206\t\n   207\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n   208\t  step Alex opens.\n   209\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\nPASS  ledger-stop: after the ledger stops, nothing more is sent  5 attempts, 31 not sent\nPASS  separate-agree-float: Q3 forecasts equal within floating-point error are unified, and the pair reconciles  []\nPASS  packets: a reconciled card is shown with its own original derivation, not the unified copy  P11\nPASS  packets: the scoring packet shows the final answer; the refused first answer is only in the unscored attempts file, unlinked  P21\nPASS  one-transport: a request that fails in transport is final as transport, not published  \nPASS  verdict: a unit failed in transport makes the verdict INCOMPLETE  single-E|single|1: transport; P11 K1 usable: reader A gave no yes/no with a ground from this packet\nPASS  interrupt: results are written from the records; the unit in flight is interrupted, the rest not sent  {'pair-old-2|joint|1': 'publish', 'pair-old-2|joint|2': 'not sent', 'pair-old-2|joint|3': 'not sent'}\nPASS  separate-within-dup: two equal forecasts inside one answer are kept, so the reconciled pair is refused as the joint one is (C3)  refused / joint unresolved\nPASS  separate-within-dup-shared: two equal shared forecasts within one call are not unified with each other, so C4 refuses as within one call  refused [\"('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3') base: 3 forecast nodes (v14.q3_two_a, v14.q3_two_b, v9.q3_one_v9); exactly one per scenario is required\"]\nPASS  separate-within-dup-second: the second call's two equal shared forecasts are not both unified to the first call's one (C4 refuses)  refused [\"('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3') base: 3 forecast nodes (v14.q3_one_v14, v9.q3_two_a, v9.q3_two_b); exactly one per scenario is required\"]\nPASS  abstain: an unresolved singleton is published and can be read with its card as the ground  \nPASS  verdict: a swap of two packets with identical text: INCOMPLETE (the key is not the committed one)  the key is not the one packets.md committed to\nPASS  verdict: decisions written into the key: INCOMPLETE (the key is not the committed one)  INCOMPLETE\nPASS  torn journal: recover keeps the committed entries, marks the torn attempt interrupted and the line damaged, sends nothing  single-E|single|3: interrupted\nPASS  torn journal: the interrupted card's packet says the request was started and no answer recorded  P06\nPASS  verdict: a damaged journal line makes the verdict INCOMPLETE  answers.jsonl line 72 is damaged\nPASS  a refused first answer whose retry was never sent is incomplete, not refused or not sent  \n51 of 51 checks pass\nCAUGHT  12 a reconciled card shows the merged calculation  FAIL  packets: a reconciled card is shown with its own original derivation, not the unified copy  P18\nCAUGHT  13 the scoring packet shows the first attempt  FAIL  packets: the scoring packet shows the final answer; the refused first answer is only in the unscored att\nCAUGHT  14 a several-candidate first call is unified  FAIL  separate-within-dup-shared: two equal shared forecasts within one call are not unified with each other, \nCAUGHT  15 a several-candidate second call is unified  FAIL  separate-within-dup-second: the second call's two equal shared forecasts are not both unified to the fir\nCAUGHT  16 the commitment is not checked  FAIL  verdict: a swap of two packets with identical text: INCOMPLETE (the key is not the committed one)  packe\nCAUGHT  17 an interrupted card reads as never sent  FAIL  torn journal: the interrupted card's packet says the request was started and no answer recorded  P08\nCAUGHT  18 a card is not a ground  FAIL  abstain: an unresolved singleton is published and can be read with its card as the ground  P02 K1 usable\nCAUGHT  19 a torn journal line stops the summary  crash: json.decoder.JSONDecodeError: Expecting ',' delimiter: line 1 column 532 (char 531)\nCAUGHT  20 a damaged line does not make the verdict incomplete  FAIL  verdict: a damaged journal line makes the verdict INCOMPLETE  single-E|single|3: interrupted\n20 of 20 mutants caught; control passes\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
