{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '149,227p'; nl -ba RESULT.md | sed -n '73,103p'; rg -n 'def publish_decision|unit.*USD|def _key|C4' calc_check.py\"","aggregated_output":"   149\t## 3e. After council round 47d (`codex-r47d.md`): three structural rules\n   150\t\n   151\tRounds 47b to 47d kept finding the same two things: process information inside the readers' packets, and a mapping from packets to\n   152\tunits that could change after reading. These findings were answered by rule, not one by one.\n   153\t\n   154\t1. **The scoring text holds only what the four questions need.** For each card: the question, the ladder, the passages it names,\n   155\t   its own figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. It carries no attempt history, no code decision\n   156\t   and no check code. The verdict applies the code's decision itself.\n   157\t   - Earlier attempts go to `attempts.md`. That file is for diagnostic reading only and is never scored. Each attempt sits under its\n   158\t     own shuffled label (D01, …), with no link to a packet. [47d.3]\n   159\t   - A card with no final answer says why in plain words: no request was sent; the request was started and no answer was recorded;\n   160\t     no answer arrived; the answer was refused and its retry was not sent; or the answer did not match the format. [47d.4]\n   161\t2. **The text the readers receive commits to the mapping.** The key is {a random salt, the run's digest, the packet order, the\n   162\t   attempt labels}. Its sha256 is the first line of `packets.md`. The verdict refuses a key whose sha256 differs from that line. It\n   163\t   also renders the packets again from the run and the key, and refuses a mismatch with `packets.md` or with the readings' sha256.\n   164\t   A swap of two packets with identical text is caught, and so is a decision written into the key. [47d.1]\n   165\t3. **Reconciliation is one to one.** A declared shared forecast is unified only when each of the two calls holds exactly one\n   166\t   candidate for that quantity and scenario, and their values are the same. Otherwise every copy stays, for C3 and C4 to judge as in a\n   167\t   joint answer. [47d.2]\n   168\t\n   169\t- **The record:** an attempt that was started and not finished is kept in `results.json` as interrupted.\n   170\t- **Rehearsal:** 51 of 51, three times (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n   171\t  - the scoring text has no attempt, decision or code;\n   172\t  - the refused first answer appears only in `attempts.md`;\n   173\t  - a swap of identical-text packets is INCOMPLETE;\n   174\t  - a forged key is INCOMPLETE;\n   175\t  - two equal shared forecasts in the second call are refused (C4, three nodes);\n   176\t  - an interrupted card says the request was started.\n   177\t- **Mutants:** 20 of 20 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   178\t\n   179\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   180\t\n   181\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   182\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   183\t  - Each packet shows, per card (K1, K2), the question, the ladder, every passage the final answer names (as the request showed it),\n   184\t    its figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. Nothing about attempts or the code's decision is\n   185\t    shown (§3e).\n   186\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. The verdict, not the reader, applies the code's\n   187\t    decision: its cards cannot count as usable.\n   188\t  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n   189\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   190\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   191\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   192\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   193\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   194\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   195\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   196\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   197\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines):\n   198\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   199\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   200\t    singleton answers.\n   201\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   202\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n   203\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n   204\t\n   205\t## 5. What the result decides\n   206\t\n   207\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n   208\t  step Alex opens.\n   209\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n    73\t## The interim for a first release\n    74\t\n    75\tPublish questions, evidence and events, and show number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the forecast text and its\n    76\thistory withheld together (`bundle.py`).\n    77\t\n    78\t## The one test (registered with the design)\n    79\t\n    80\t- **The $0 gate.** Hand-reconstruct, in the new format:\n    81\t  - old-2 8729/8737, 8734 and 8595, and old-3 9166;\n    82\t  - the four gold controls;\n    83\t  - three planted errors (an amount absent from its quote, a wrong sum, an internal forecast labelled consensus).\n    84\t\n    85\t  The format must expose every defect, represent every control, and fail every plant. Any miss stops the line.\n    86\t- **The paid gate** (Alex's ceiling; 36 calls, about $0.2–0.4 estimated):\n    87\t  - **The arms:** the 09-20 total and Data Center pair in each draw, three samples each, judged jointly and separately under the same\n    88\t    format and checks. Plus three samples each on the O, S and E requests. Every output is read against its source with the arm\n    89\t    hidden.\n    90\t  - **Pass:** the joint arm publishes both answers usable and source-supported in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot,\n    91\t    and at least 3 more usable pairs than the separate arm. Zero published hard contradictions, internal-as-market references, or\n    92\t    unresolved overlap, scope or unsized adjustments that decide the band.\n    93\t  - **Stop:** any such published defect, either coverage line missed, or an incomplete comparison.\n8:Values are in the figure's unit; money is normalised to 'USD bn'.\n56:                item.update(midpoint=_num(g[0]) * _scale(g[1]), relative=_num(g[2]), unit='USD bn')\n59:                item.update(low=_num(g[0]) * _scale(g[1] or unit), high=_num(g[2]) * _scale(unit), unit='USD bn')\n61:                item.update(bound=QUAL[g[0].lower()], value=_num(g[1]) * _scale(g[2]), unit='USD bn')\n63:                item.update(value=_num(g[0]) * _scale(g[1]), unit='USD bn')\n65:                item.update(value=_num(g[0]), unit='USD')\n93:        ok = _same(fig.get('value'), expr['midpoint']) and unit == 'USD bn' and bound is None\n97:        ok = _same(fig.get('value'), expr[comp]) and unit == 'USD bn' and bound is None\n139:        if 'units' in units and 'USD' in units and out_unit == 'USD bn':     # units times a dollar price, in billions\n144:        if 'USD' in units and 'USD bn' in units:                # a dollar total over a per-unit price\n298:def _key(what):\n524:            errors.append(('C4', f'{f[\"id\"]} ({sc}) rests on estimates of another scenario ({\", \".join(sorted(other))})'))\n529:                errors.append(('C4', f'{rel[\"part\"]} covers scenarios {sorted(sp)} but {rel[\"whole\"]} covers {sorted(sw)}; related members cover the same'))\n538:            errors.append(('C4', f'{f[\"id\"]}: a range summary must be an estimate with low and high that is an answer\\'s outcome and feeds no figure'\n541:    # C3 part within whole, C4 one forecast per shared quantity (every path)\n582:            errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: no forecast node, though {\", \".join(touched)} depend on it'))\n585:                errors.append(('C4', f'{want} {sc}: {len(ids)} forecast nodes ({\", \".join(ids)}); exactly one per scenario is required'))\n594:                errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: {f[\"id\"]} ({sc}) depends on {\", \".join(borrowed)} of another scenario'))\n598:                errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: {view_id} reaches {\", \".join(sorted(bypass))} without passing a forecast node ({\", \".join(sorted(stop))})'))\n672:    price = [i for i in ins if i['what']['measure'] == 'price per unit' and i['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')]\n674:        return same and len(price) == 1 and ins[1] is price[0] and out['measure'] == 'units' and ins[0]['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')\n676:    return same and len(price) == 1 and len(units) == 1 and fig['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')\n732:def publish_decision(family, calc, result):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'def r1|samedup|separate-within|abstain|packets|usable' gate.py paid_rehearsal.py | tail -40; sed -n '1,140p' paid_gate.py\"","aggregated_output":"paid_rehearsal.py:294:    check('verdict: joint 9, separate 5: PASS', v['verdict'] == 'PASS', str(v['separate usable pairs']))\npaid_rehearsal.py:304:    v = verdict_of(readings(5, disagree={'usable': yes('yes')}), 'third-decides')\npaid_rehearsal.py:309:    v = verdict_of(readings(5), 'other-packets', packets_sha='0' * 64)\npaid_rehearsal.py:310:    check('verdict: readings made on other packets: INCOMPLETE', v['verdict'] == 'INCOMPLETE', '; '.join(v['problems'][:1]))\npaid_rehearsal.py:316:    check('verdict: a run changed after the packets were frozen: INCOMPLETE', v['verdict'] == 'INCOMPLETE' and any('does not belong' in x for x in v['problems']),\npaid_rehearsal.py:383:    pg.packets(scratch / 'separate-agree-float', fkeys)\npaid_rehearsal.py:384:    fkey = pg.render_packets(scratch / 'separate-agree-float', json.loads((fkeys / 'packet-key.json').read_text()))[1]\npaid_rehearsal.py:386:    section = (scratch / 'separate-agree-float' / 'packets.md').read_text().split(f'## {pid}\\n')[1].split('\\n## ')[0]\npaid_rehearsal.py:387:    check('packets: a reconciled card is shown with its own original derivation, not the unified copy',\npaid_rehearsal.py:391:    pg.packets(scratch / 'retry', rkeys)\npaid_rehearsal.py:393:    rkey = pg.render_packets(scratch / 'retry', rfrozen)[1]\npaid_rehearsal.py:395:    section = (scratch / 'retry' / 'packets.md').read_text().split(f'## {pid}\\n')[1].split('\\n## ')[0]\npaid_rehearsal.py:397:    check('packets: the scoring packet shows the final answer; the refused first answer is only in the unscored attempts file, unlinked',\npaid_rehearsal.py:404:    pg.packets(scratch / 'one-transport', tkeys)\npaid_rehearsal.py:406:    rd = {pid: {c: card() for c in k['cards']} for pid, k in pg.render_packets(scratch / 'one-transport', tfrozen)[1].items()}\npaid_rehearsal.py:407:    v = verdict_of(rd, 'transport', out=scratch / 'one-transport', keys=tkeys, packets_sha=pg.hashlib.sha256((scratch / 'one-transport' / 'packets.md').read_bytes()).hexdigest())\npaid_rehearsal.py:418:    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'separate-within-dup')\npaid_rehearsal.py:420:    check('separate-within-dup: two equal forecasts inside one answer are kept, so the reconciled pair is refused as the joint one is (C3)',\npaid_rehearsal.py:423:    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'separate-within-dup-shared')\npaid_rehearsal.py:425:    check('separate-within-dup-shared: two equal shared forecasts within one call are not unified with each other, so C4 refuses as within one call',\npaid_rehearsal.py:428:    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'separate-within-dup-second')\npaid_rehearsal.py:430:    check('separate-within-dup-second: the second call\\'s two equal shared forecasts are not both unified to the first call\\'s one (C4 refuses)',\npaid_rehearsal.py:434:    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'abstain')\npaid_rehearsal.py:435:    akeys = scratch / 'key-abstain'\npaid_rehearsal.py:436:    pg.packets(scratch / 'abstain', akeys)\npaid_rehearsal.py:438:    arend = pg.render_packets(scratch / 'abstain', afrozen)[1]\npaid_rehearsal.py:441:    for pid, k in arend.items():                            # every draw of single-S abstains\npaid_rehearsal.py:444:    v = verdict_of(rd, 'abstain', out=scratch / 'abstain', keys=akeys, packets_sha=pg.hashlib.sha256((scratch / 'abstain' / 'packets.md').read_bytes()).hexdigest())\npaid_rehearsal.py:445:    check('abstain: an unresolved singleton is published and can be read with its card as the ground', s['finals']['single-S|single|1']['decision'] == 'publish'\npaid_rehearsal.py:447:    # [47c.2, 47d.1] the key orders the packets, and the readers' text commits to it: a swap of two packets whose text is identical\npaid_rehearsal.py:453:    same_text = pg.render_packets(scratch / 'clean', swapped)[0].split('\\n', 1)[1] == text.split('\\n', 1)[1]\npaid_rehearsal.py:455:    check('verdict: a swap of two packets with identical text: INCOMPLETE (the key is not the committed one)', same_text and v['verdict'] == 'INCOMPLETE'\npaid_rehearsal.py:457:    claimed = dict(frozen, packets={pid: {'decision': 'held'} for pid, _ in frozen['order']})\npaid_rehearsal.py:464:    shutil.copytree(scratch / 'clean', scratch / 'torn', ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns('packets.md', 'attempts.md', 'results.json'))\npaid_rehearsal.py:479:    pg.packets(scratch / 'torn', tk)\npaid_rehearsal.py:481:    trend = pg.render_packets(scratch / 'torn', tf)[1]\npaid_rehearsal.py:483:    v = verdict_of(rd, 'torn', out=scratch / 'torn', keys=tk, packets_sha=pg.hashlib.sha256((scratch / 'torn' / 'packets.md').read_bytes()).hexdigest())\npaid_rehearsal.py:485:    tsection = (scratch / 'torn' / 'packets.md').read_text().split(f'## {tpid}\\n')[1].split('\\n## ')[0]\ngate.py:73:def r1_common():\ngate.py:93:def r1(variant):\n\"\"\"The paid gate of judging-v13 (D725's registered test; D729, D730). Harness-only; nothing here is product code.\n\n  python3 paid_gate.py plan <out.json>                        # $0: build every request from the stored runs and check them\n  python3 paid_gate.py send <new out folder> <ceiling>        # paid: only at the ceiling Alex names (APPROVED_CEILING)\n  python3 paid_gate.py packets <out folder> <key folder>      # $0: blind reading packets, the arm hidden; the key kept outside the repo\n  python3 paid_gate.py verdict <out folder> <readings.json> <key folder>   # $0: the registered pass and stop lines\n\nThe test (D725, RESULT.md): the 09-20 total and Data Center pair in each of three stored draws, judged jointly (one v13 family call)\nand separately (each member alone, the same union of evidence, the same v13 format), three samples each; plus three samples each of\nthe O, S and E singletons. 9 + 18 + 9 = 36 first attempts. A calculation the checks refuse is retried once with its errors; a second\nrefusal makes the unit unresolved. The separate arm's two answers are then reconciled by the same checks over the pair's family.\n\"\"\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport random\nimport re\nimport secrets\nimport sqlite3\nimport sys\nimport threading\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parents[2]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\nsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\nimport calc_check as cc                                                 # noqa: E402\nimport render_v13 as rv                                                 # noqa: E402\nfrom hivemind import config, model                                      # noqa: E402\n\nRUN = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\nCONFIG = REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'                              # its re-judging model setting: gpt-6-luna, medium, 16000 output tokens\nSYSTEM = (HERE / 'judging-v13-draft.txt').read_text()\nAPPROVED_CEILING = None                                                 # set only from Alex's answer; send refuses while None\nPINNED_PLAN_SHA256 = (HERE / 'paid-plan.sha256').read_text().strip() if (HERE / 'paid-plan.sha256').exists() else None\nAUTH = Path.home() / '.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/authorization.json'\nDRAWS = (1, 2, 3)\nRETRY_MARK = '\\n\\nThe code refused the previous answer because: '\nPAIRS = [('old-1', ('v4', 9014), ('v8', 9022)), ('old-2', ('v14', 8729), ('v9', 8737)), ('old-3', ('v3', 9183), ('v35', 9177))]\nSINGLETONS = [('O', 'old-2', 'v29', 8734, ('NVIDIA', 'equity investment commitments', 'company', 'end of FY2027')),\n              ('S', 'old-2', 'v6', 8595, ('four largest AI hyperscalers', 'data-center capex', 'combined', 'CY2027')),\n              ('E', 'old-3', 'v41', 9166, ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Vera CPU', 'FY2028'))]\n\n\ndef W(population, measure, scope, period):\n    return {'population': population, 'measure': measure, 'scope': scope, 'period': period}\n\n\ndef bands(draw, view_id):\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    rows = conn.execute('select lo, hi from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,)).fetchall()\n    return [[lo / 1e9 if lo is not None else None, hi / 1e9 if hi is not None else None] for lo, hi in rows]\n\n\ndef passages(draw, evidence_ids):\n    \"\"\"What each request showed of a passage: the quote cut at 400 characters (judging._lines_english).\"\"\"\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    rows = conn.execute(f'select evidence_id, quote, speaker from evidence where evidence_id in ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(evidence_ids))})',\n                        evidence_ids).fetchall()\n    return {e: {'text': (q or '')[:400], 'speaker': s} for e, q, s in rows}\n\n\ndef pair_family(draw, total, dc):\n    return {'members': {total[0]: {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027'), 'bands': bands(draw, total[0])},\n                        dc[0]: {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'bands': bands(draw, dc[0])}},\n            'relations': [{'type': 'part_of', 'part': dc[0], 'whole': total[0]}],\n            'shared': [W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'), W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q4')],\n            'compare_periods': ['FY2027 Q3', 'FY2027 Q4', 'FY2027']}\n\n\ndef only(family, view_id):\n    return {'members': {view_id: family['members'][view_id]}, 'relations': [], 'shared': family['shared'], 'compare_periods': []}\n\n\ndef questions(draw, view_ids):\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    out = {}\n    for v in view_ids:\n        q = conn.execute('select question from views where view_id=?', (v,)).fetchone()[0]\n        ladder = [c for (c,) in conn.execute('select condition from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (v,))]\n        out[v] = {'question': q, 'ladder': ladder}\n    return out\n\n\ndef shown_lines(user):\n    \"\"\"Each evidence item exactly as the request showed it: its header line (tier, speaker, original source and date) and its quote.\"\"\"\n    m = re.search(r'\\[Evidence in view for the family, \\d+ items\\]\\n(.*?)(?:\\n\\n\\[|\\n\\nAnswer per)', user, re.S)\n    out = {}\n    for chunk in re.split(r'\\n(?=- e\\d+ )', m.group(1) if m else ''):\n        if chunk.startswith('- e'):\n            out[chunk[2:].split(' ', 1)[0]] = chunk\n    return out\n\n\ndef item(unit, arm, draw, calls, family, shown):\n    archive = RUN / draw / 'prod/archive.sqlite'\n    user, evidence_ids, theme_ids = rv.render(archive, calls, family, shown=shown)\n    return {'unit': unit, 'arm': arm, 'draw_store': draw, 'members': sorted(shown), 'system': SYSTEM, 'user': user,\n            'schema': rv.v13_schema(sorted(shown), evidence_ids, theme_ids), 'family': family, 'passages': passages(draw, evidence_ids),\n            'evidence_ids': evidence_ids, 'questions': questions(draw, sorted(shown)), 'shown': shown_lines(user)}\n\n\ndef build_plan():\n    items = []\n    for draw, total, dc in PAIRS:\n        family = pair_family(draw, total, dc)\n        calls = [total, dc]\n        items.append(item(f'pair-{draw}', 'joint', draw, calls, family, [total[0], dc[0]]))\n        for member in (total, dc):                            # the same union of evidence, one member's header and answer\n            items.append(item(f'pair-{draw}', f'separate-{member[0]}', draw, calls, only(family, member[0]), [member[0]]))\n    for name, draw, view_id, call_id, what in SINGLETONS:\n        family = {'members': {view_id: {'what': W(*what), 'bands': bands(draw, view_id)}}, 'relations': [], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': []}\n        items.append(item(f'single-{name}', 'single', draw, [(view_id, call_id)], family, [view_id]))\n    return items\n\n\ndef plan(out):\n    items = build_plan()\n    report = []\n    for it in items:\n        missing = sorted(set(it['evidence_ids']) - set(it['passages']))\n        report.append(f'{it[\"unit\"]:14} {it[\"arm\"]:14} members {it[\"members\"]} user {len(it[\"user\"])} chars, evidence {len(it[\"evidence_ids\"])}, '\n                      f'schema {len(json.dumps(it[\"schema\"]))} chars, passages missing {missing or \"none\"}')\n        if missing or 'Outcome keys' not in it['user']:\n            raise SystemExit(f'{it[\"unit\"]} {it[\"arm\"]}: incomplete request; not planned')\n    ids = [(i['unit'], i['arm']) for i in items]\n    if len(set(ids)) != len(ids):\n        raise SystemExit('duplicate (unit, arm) in the plan; not planned')\n    text = json.dumps(items, indent=1)\n    Path(out).write_text(text)\n    Path(out).with_suffix('.sha256').write_text(hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest() + '\\n')\n    print('\\n'.join(report))\n    print(f'{len(items)} requests x {len(DRAWS)} draws = {len(items) * len(DRAWS)} first attempts')\n\n\ndef strip(data):\n    return rv.without_nulls(data)\n\n\nclass Gate:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba calc_check.py | sed -n '297,310p;391,435p;540,601p;644,683p;722,762p'; nl -ba gate.py | sed -n '18,150p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba calc_check.py | sed -n '297,310p;391,435p;540,601p;644,683p;722,762p'; nl -ba gate.py | sed -n '18,150p'\"","aggregated_output":"   297\t\n   298\tdef _key(what):\n   299\t    return (what['population'], what['measure'], what['scope'], what['period'])\n   300\t\n   301\t\n   302\tdef check(family, passages, calc):\n   303\t    errors, recorded = [], []\n   304\t    figs = {}\n   305\t    for fig in calc['figures']:\n   306\t        if fig['id'] in figs:\n   307\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]} is defined twice'))\n   308\t        figs[fig['id']] = fig\n   309\t\n   310\t    def refs(fig):\n   391\t        if want == 'mixed':\n   392\t            errors.append(('C2', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: its inputs are bounded on opposite sides, so its value is unbounded; state it as an estimate'))\n   393\t        elif want is not None and have != want:\n   394\t            errors.append(('C2', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: its inputs make it a {want} bound, but it is declared {fig.get(\"bound\") or \"a point\"}'))\n   395\t        elif want is None and fig.get('bound'):\n   396\t            errors.append(('C2', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: its inputs are points, but it is declared a bound ({fig[\"bound\"]})'))\n   397\t\n   398\t    # C8 operand compatibility\n   399\t    for fig in figs.values():\n   400\t        if fig['kind'] != 'computed' or fig.get('operation') not in OPERATIONS:\n   401\t            continue\n   402\t        ins = [figs[i] for i in fig['inputs'] if i in figs]\n   403\t        op, rel, out = fig['operation'], fig.get('relation'), fig['what']\n   404\t        differing = [i['id'] for i in ins if i['unit'] not in ('%', 'x') and\n   405\t                     (i['what']['population'], i['what']['scope'], i['what']['period'], i['what']['measure']) !=\n   406\t                     (out['population'], out['scope'], out['period'], out['measure'])]\n   407\t        if op in ('sum', 'difference'):\n   408\t            money = [i for i in ins if i['unit'] not in ('%', 'x')]\n   409\t            same_qty = all((i['what']['population'], i['what']['measure'], i['what']['scope']) ==\n   410\t                           (out['population'], out['measure'], out['scope']) for i in money)\n   411\t            if rel == 'time_aggregation':\n   412\t                qs = [_quarters(i['what']['period']) for i in money]\n   413\t                q_out = _quarters(out['period'])\n   414\t                union = set().union(*[q[1] for q in qs]) if all(qs) else None\n   415\t                disjoint = all(qs) and sum(len(q[1]) for q in qs) == len(union or ())\n   416\t                if not (same_qty and q_out and all(qs) and disjoint and union == q_out[1] and all(q[0] == q_out[0] for q in qs)):\n   417\t                    errors.append(('C8', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: time aggregation needs one quantity over disjoint periods forming {out[\"period\"]}'))\n   418\t            elif rel in ('overlap_unknown', 'stated_in_addition'):\n   419\t                if rel == 'overlap_unknown' and fig.get('disputed') not in fig['inputs']:\n   420\t                    errors.append(('C8', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: overlap_unknown must name a disputed operand among its inputs'))\n   421\t            elif rel == 'accounting_parts':\n   422\t                wholes = {(r['whole_scope'], tuple(r['part_scopes'])) for r in family.get('scope_parts', [])}\n   423\t                if not any(out['scope'] == w and all(i['what']['scope'] in p for i in money) for w, p in wholes):\n   424\t                    errors.append(('C8', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: accounting_parts needs a declared split of {out[\"scope\"]}'))\n   425\t            elif differing:\n   426\t                errors.append(('C8', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: {op} of different quantities or periods ({\", \".join(differing)}) states no relation'))\n   427\t        elif op == 'roll_forward':\n   428\t            opening = ins[0]['what']['period'] if ins else ''\n   429\t            if not (opening.startswith('as of') and all(not i['what']['period'].startswith('as of') for i in ins[1:])\n   430\t                    and out['period'].startswith(('as of', 'end of'))):\n   431\t                errors.append(('C8', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: roll_forward needs an opening balance as of a date, flows after it, and a closing balance'))\n   432\t            if rel == 'overlap_unknown' and fig.get('disputed') not in fig['inputs']:\n   433\t                errors.append(('C8', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: overlap_unknown must name a disputed operand among its inputs'))\n   434\t        elif op == 'share':\n   435\t            pct = [i for i in ins if i['unit'] == '%']\n   540\t\n   541\t    # C3 part within whole, C4 one forecast per shared quantity (every path)\n   542\t    def reachable(start, stop=None):\n   543\t        stops = set(stop) if isinstance(stop, (set, list, tuple)) else {stop}\n   544\t        seen_ids, stack = set(), [start]\n   545\t        while stack:\n   546\t            fid = stack.pop()\n   547\t            if fid in seen_ids or fid not in figs:\n   548\t                continue\n   549\t            seen_ids.add(fid)\n   550\t            if fid not in stops:\n   551\t                stack.extend(refs(figs[fid]))\n   552\t        return seen_ids\n   553\t    scenarios = {f.get('scenario', 'base') for f in figs.values() if f['basis'] == 'forecast'} or {'base'}\n   554\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):\n   555\t        if rel['type'] != 'part_of' or rel['part'] not in outcomes or rel['whole'] not in outcomes:\n   556\t            continue\n   557\t        part_m, whole_m = members[rel['part']], members[rel['whole']]\n   558\t        for sc in scenarios:\n   559\t            for period in family.get('compare_periods', []):\n   560\t                def node(view_id, member):\n   561\t                    want = (member['what']['population'], member['what']['measure'], member['what']['scope'], period)\n   562\t                    hits = sorted((figs[f] for f in reachable(outcomes[view_id]) if _key(figs[f]['what']) == want\n   563\t                                   and figs[f]['basis'] == 'forecast' and figs[f].get('scenario', 'base') == sc), key=lambda f: f['id'])\n   564\t                    if len(hits) > 1:                 # [46x.1] one forecast per member quantity, period and scenario\n   565\t                        errors.append(('C3', f'{period} {sc}: {view_id} has {len(hits)} forecasts ({\", \".join(f[\"id\"] for f in hits)}); '\n   566\t                                             'the comparison is ambiguous'))\n   567\t                        return None\n   568\t                    return hits[0] if hits else None\n   569\t                p, w = node(rel['part'], part_m), node(rel['whole'], whole_m)\n   570\t                if p and w and _exceeds(_outcome_set(p), _outcome_set(w)):          # [46s] open and closed ends kept\n   571\t                    errors.append(('C3', f'{period} {sc}: {rel[\"part\"]} {p[\"id\"]} {_outcome_set(p)} exceeds {rel[\"whole\"]} {w[\"id\"]} {_outcome_set(w)}'))\n   572\t    for shared in family.get('shared', []):\n   573\t        want = _key(shared)\n   574\t        nodes = [f for f in figs.values() if _key(f['what']) == want and f['basis'] == 'forecast']\n   575\t        touched = [v for v, o in outcomes.items() if any(_key(figs[f]['what']) == want for f in reachable(o))]\n   576\t        if not touched:\n   577\t            continue\n   578\t        per_scenario = {}\n   579\t        for n in nodes:\n   580\t            per_scenario.setdefault(n.get('scenario', 'base'), []).append(n['id'])\n   581\t        if not nodes:\n   582\t            errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: no forecast node, though {\", \".join(touched)} depend on it'))\n   583\t        for sc, ids in sorted(per_scenario.items()):\n   584\t            if len(ids) != 1:\n   585\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want} {sc}: {len(ids)} forecast nodes ({\", \".join(ids)}); exactly one per scenario is required'))\n   586\t        stop = {n['id'] for n in nodes}\n   587\t        for f in figs.values():                       # [46i.1] scenario membership is derived along the whole path, not declared\n   588\t            sc = f.get('scenario', 'base')\n   589\t            if sc == 'range' or f['kind'] not in ('computed', 'estimate'):\n   590\t                continue\n   591\t            upstream = _upstream_of(f['id'], figs, refs)\n   592\t            borrowed = sorted(r for r in upstream if r in stop and figs[r].get('scenario', 'base') != sc)\n   593\t            if borrowed:\n   594\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: {f[\"id\"]} ({sc}) depends on {\", \".join(borrowed)} of another scenario'))\n   595\t        for view_id in touched:                      # [46g.3] a bypass reaches the quantity through no forecast node of any scenario\n   596\t            bypass = [f for f in reachable(outcomes[view_id], stop=stop) if f not in stop and _key(figs[f]['what']) == want]\n   597\t            if bypass:\n   598\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: {view_id} reaches {\", \".join(sorted(bypass))} without passing a forecast node ({\", \".join(sorted(stop))})'))\n   599\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):           # [46j.2] the later member rests on the earlier member's forecast nodes, per scenario\n   600\t        if rel['type'] != 'same_base' or rel['later'] not in outcomes or rel['earlier'] not in outcomes:\n   601\t            continue\n   644\t        earlier = fig['kind'] == 'prior' or fig.get('basis') == 'prior_forecast' or 'pointer' in fig   # [46i.2] derived, not labelled\n   645\t        if not earlier:\n   646\t            continue\n   647\t        if fig['kind'] != 'prior' or fig.get('basis') != 'prior_forecast':\n   648\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: an earlier forecast must be kind prior with basis prior_forecast'))\n   649\t        ptr, ans_prior = fig.get('pointer', {}), supplied.get(fig.get('pointer', {}).get('view'), {})\n   650\t        if ans_prior.get('day') != ptr.get('day') or not any(_same(fig.get('value'), v) for v in ans_prior.get('values', [])):\n   651\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: no earlier answer of {ptr.get(\"view\")} on {ptr.get(\"day\")} shown in the request states {fig.get(\"value\")}'))\n   652\t        owners = [a['view_id'] for a in calc['answers'] if a.get('outcome') == fig['id']]\n   653\t        if owners:                                    # [46h.2] nor the current outcome\n   654\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: an earlier forecast cannot be the current outcome of {\", \".join(owners)}'))\n   655\t        users = [f['id'] for f in figs.values() if fig['id'] in refs(f)]\n   656\t        if users:\n   657\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: an earlier forecast is for comparison only and cannot feed {\", \".join(users)}'))\n   658\t\n   659\t    recorded += _assumptions(family, figs, outcomes, calc, refs)\n   660\t    finite = lambda v: v if abs(v) != float('inf') else None\n   661\t    published = {v: [finite(_outcome_set(figs[o])[0]), finite(_outcome_set(figs[o])[2]), figs[o].get('bound')] for v, o in outcomes.items()}\n   662\t    return {'errors': errors, 'recorded': recorded, 'published': published}\n   663\t\n   664\t\n   665\tdef _per_unit(op, ins, fig):\n   666\t    \"\"\"The per-unit identity: ratio(total, price per unit) -> units, product(units, price per unit) -> total, for one population and\n   667\t    scope. Labels are the judge's; a reader checks them against the passages.\"\"\"\n   668\t    out = fig['what']\n   669\t    if len(ins) != 2:\n   670\t        return False\n   671\t    same = all((i['what']['population'], i['what']['scope']) == (out['population'], out['scope']) for i in ins)\n   672\t    price = [i for i in ins if i['what']['measure'] == 'price per unit' and i['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')]\n   673\t    if op == 'ratio':\n   674\t        return same and len(price) == 1 and ins[1] is price[0] and out['measure'] == 'units' and ins[0]['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')\n   675\t    units = [i for i in ins if i['what']['measure'] == 'units' and i['unit'] == 'units']\n   676\t    return same and len(price) == 1 and len(units) == 1 and fig['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')\n   677\t\n   678\t\n   679\tdef member_sources(answer, figs):\n   680\t    \"\"\"[46k.3, 46ac.1] The source figures a member's own outcome and reference rest on, each identified by its passage, expression and\n   681\t    the component used.\"\"\"\n   682\t    refs = lambda f: list(f.get('inputs', [])) + [r for r in f.get('rests_on', []) if r in figs] + \\\n   683\t        ([f['adjusts']['figure']] if f.get('adjusts') else []) + ([f['bridge']] if f.get('bridge') else [])\n   722\t    prev = (finite(prev[0]), finite(prev[1]), prev[2])\n   723\t    near = lambda a, b: (a is None and b is None) or (a is not None and b is not None and abs(a - b) <= 0.005 * max(abs(b), 1e-9))\n   724\t    if cur[2] != prev[2] or not near(cur[0], prev[0]) or not near(cur[1], prev[1]):\n   725\t        reasons.append(f'outcome {list(prev)} to {list(cur)}')\n   726\t    added, dropped = sorted(set(sources) - set(previous['sources'])), sorted(set(previous['sources']) - set(sources))\n   727\t    if added or dropped:\n   728\t        reasons.append(f'source figures added {added}, dropped {dropped}')\n   729\t    return bool(reasons), '; '.join(reasons) or 'unchanged'\n   730\t\n   731\t\n   732\tdef publish_decision(family, calc, result):\n   733\t    \"\"\"DESIGN.md §4: 'refused' when a check fails (the harness retries once); 'held' when a member is unresolved and a declared\n   734\t    relation joins it to another member; else 'publish' (unresolved members shown as unresolved).\"\"\"\n   735\t    if result['errors']:\n   736\t        return 'refused'\n   737\t    unresolved = {a['view_id'] for a in calc['answers'] if a.get('shape') == 'unresolved'}\n   738\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):\n   739\t        ends = {rel.get('part'), rel.get('whole'), rel.get('later'), rel.get('earlier')} - {None}\n   740\t        if ends & unresolved and ends - unresolved:\n   741\t            return 'held'\n   742\t    return 'publish'\n   743\t\n   744\t\n   745\tdef family_outcome(attempts):\n   746\t    \"\"\"The round's outcome from up to two attempts' decisions: a refusal is retried once; two refusals make the family unresolved.\"\"\"\n   747\t    if attempts[0] != 'refused':\n   748\t        return attempts[0]\n   749\t    if len(attempts) > 1 and attempts[1] != 'refused':\n   750\t        return attempts[1]\n   751\t    return 'unresolved'\n   752\t\n   753\t\n   754\tdef _determining(fid, figs):\n   755\t    \"\"\"The figures that determine fid's value: computed inputs only, at any depth (an estimate's rests_on explains, it does not compute).\"\"\"\n   756\t    seen_ids, stack = set(), list(figs[fid].get('inputs', [])) if figs[fid]['kind'] == 'computed' else []\n   757\t    while stack:\n   758\t        f = stack.pop()\n   759\t        if f in seen_ids or f not in figs:\n   760\t            continue\n   761\t        seen_ids.add(f)\n   762\t        if figs[f]['kind'] == 'computed':\n    18\tdef store_passages(draw, ids):\n    19\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    20\t    rows = conn.execute(f'select evidence_id, quote, speaker from evidence where evidence_id in ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(ids))})', ids).fetchall()\n    21\t    assert len(rows) == len(ids), (draw, ids, rows)\n    22\t    return {e: {'text': q, 'speaker': s} for e, q, s in rows}\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\tdef packet_passages(ids):\n    26\t    items = {it['id']: it for it in json.loads(PACKET.read_text())['items']}\n    27\t    return {i: {'text': items[i]['passage'], 'speaker': items[i]['who']} for i in ids}\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\tdef W(population, measure, scope, period):\n    31\t    return {'population': population, 'measure': measure, 'scope': scope, 'period': period}\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\tdef src(fid, evidence, expression, value, unit, basis, what, component='value', bound=None):\n    35\t    fig = {'id': fid, 'kind': 'source', 'evidence': evidence, 'expression': expression, 'component': component, 'value': value,\n    36\t           'unit': unit, 'basis': basis, 'what': what}\n    37\t    if bound:\n    38\t        fig['bound'] = bound\n    39\t    return fig\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef comp(fid, op, inputs, value, unit, what, basis='forecast', **extra):\n    43\t    fig = {'id': fid, 'kind': 'computed', 'operation': op, 'inputs': inputs, 'unit': unit, 'basis': basis, 'what': what}\n    44\t    fig.update({'low': value[0], 'high': value[1]} if isinstance(value, tuple) else {'value': value})\n    45\t    fig.update(extra)\n    46\t    return fig\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tdef est(fid, value, unit, what, basis_text, rests_on=(), basis='forecast', **extra):\n    50\t    fig = {'id': fid, 'kind': 'estimate', 'unit': unit, 'basis': basis, 'what': what, 'basis_text': basis_text, 'rests_on': list(rests_on)}\n    51\t    fig.update({'low': value[0], 'high': value[1]} if isinstance(value, tuple) else {'value': value})\n    52\t    fig.update(extra)\n    53\t    return fig\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tdef ans(view_id, outcome, rung, reference):\n    57\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'shape': 'forecast', 'outcome': outcome, 'rung': rung, 'reference': reference, 'reasons': 'r', 'cites': [],\n    58\t            'pushes': [], 'theme_pushes': [], 'changed': True, 'why_changed': 'w'}\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t# ---------- R1: old-2 calls 8729 (v14) and 8737 (v9), 2026-09-20 ----------\n    62\tBANDS_OLD2_REV = [[450, None], [400, 450], [350, 400], [300, 350], [None, 300]]\n    63\tCO, DC = 'company', 'Data Center'\n    64\tR1_FAMILY = {'members': {'v14': {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'bands': BANDS_OLD2_REV},\n    65\t                         'v9': {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), 'bands': BANDS_OLD2_REV}},\n    66\t             'relations': [{'type': 'part_of', 'part': 'v9', 'whole': 'v14'}],\n    67\t             'shared': [W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q4')],\n    68\t             'compare_periods': ['FY2027 Q3', 'FY2027 Q4', 'FY2027'],\n    69\t             'prior_answers': {'v9': {'day': '2026-09-19', 'values': [414.0, 385.0, 390.0]}}}   # call 8621: reference $414B, outcome $385–390B\n    70\tR1_PASSAGES = store_passages('old-2', ['e238', 'e2497', 'e2499', 'e4762', 'e3943', 'e5056', 'e4995', 'e3219', 'e976'])\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\tdef r1_common():\n    74\t    return [\n    75\t        src('q1', 'e238', '$81.6 billion', 81.6, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q1')),\n    76\t        src('q2', 'e2497', '$96.2 billion', 96.2, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q2')),\n    77\t        src('g3', 'e2499', '$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%', 108.0, 'USD bn', 'guidance', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'midpoint'),\n    78\t        src('g3w', 'e2499', '$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%', 2.0, '%', 'guidance', W('NVIDIA', 'guidance width', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'relative'),\n    79\t        comp('g3r', 'range_from_relative', ['g3', 'g3w'], (105.84, 110.16), 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), basis='guidance'),\n    80\t        src('beat', 'e4762', '3.1%', 3.1, '%', 'third_party', W('NVIDIA', 'beat over the guidance high end', CO, 'last four quarters')),\n    81\t        est('q3f', 113.5, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'the guide high end 110.16 plus the 3.1% average beat', ['g3r', 'beat']),\n    82\t        src('g12', 'e3943', '12%', 12.0, '%', 'third_party', W('NVIDIA', 'sequential growth', CO, 'FY2027 Q3')),\n    83\t        est('carry', 12.0, '%', W('NVIDIA', 'assumption', CO, 'FY2027 Q4'), \"Q3's guided 12% sequential growth continues into Q4\", ['g12'],\n    84\t            converts=['q3f']),\n    85\t        comp('q4f', 'apply_growth', ['q3f', 'g12'], 127.1, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q4'), bridge='carry'),\n    86\t        comp('fy14', 'sum', ['q1', 'q2', 'q3f', 'q4f'], 418.4, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), relation='time_aggregation'),\n    87\t        src('c411', 'e5056', 'around $411 billion', 411.0, 'USD bn', 'consensus', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'bound', 'approx'),\n    88\t        src('dch1', 'e4995', '$164 billion', 164.0, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 H1')),\n    89\t        src('mix', 'e3219', '92.5%', 92.5, '%', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', 'Data Center share', CO, 'FY2027 Q2')),\n    90\t    ]\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\tdef r1(variant):\n    94\t    figs = r1_common()\n    95\t    if variant in ('a', 'b'):\n    96\t        figs.append(comp('dcq3', 'share', ['g3', 'mix'], 99.9, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q3')))\n    97\t    else:\n    98\t        figs.append(comp('dcq3', 'share', ['q3f', 'mix'], 105.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q3')))\n    99\t    if variant == 'a':\n   100\t        figs.append(est('dcq4', 146.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q4'),\n   101\t                        'hyperscale reacceleration, the Rubin ramp, a discounted SemiAnalysis uplift', ['e976']))\n   102\t        dcfy = 409.9\n   103\t    elif variant == 'b':\n   104\t        figs.append(est('dcq4', 115.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q4'), 'held below the company quarter', ['e976']))\n   105\t        dcfy = 378.9\n   106\t    else:\n   107\t        figs.append(comp('dcq4', 'share', ['q4f', 'mix'], 117.6, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q4')))\n   108\t        dcfy = 386.6\n   109\t    figs.append(comp('dcfy', 'sum', ['dch1', 'dcq3', 'dcq4'], dcfy, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), relation='time_aggregation'))\n   110\t    if variant == 'a':                                    # as stored: the previous conclusion's $414B called the market reference\n   111\t        figs.append({'id': 'prior414', 'kind': 'prior', 'basis': 'prior_forecast', 'value': 414.0, 'unit': 'USD bn',\n   112\t                     'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), 'pointer': {'view': 'v9', 'day': '2026-09-19'}})   # its reference field, $414B since 09-14 (call 7939)\n   113\t        v9_ref = {'figure': 'prior414'}\n   114\t    else:\n   115\t        figs.append(comp('dcref', 'share', ['c411', 'mix'], 380.2, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), basis='consensus', bound='approx'))\n   116\t        v9_ref = {'figure': 'dcref'}\n   117\t    v9_rung = 2 if dcfy >= 400 else 3\n   118\t    return {'figures': figs, 'answers': [ans('v14', 'fy14', 2, {'figure': 'c411'}), ans('v9', 'dcfy', v9_rung, v9_ref)]}\n   119\t\n   120\t\n   121\t# ---------- R2: old-2 call 8734 (v29 equity commitments) ----------\n   122\tR2_FAMILY = {'members': {'v29': {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'equity investment commitments', CO, 'end of FY2027'),\n   123\t                                 'bands': [[None, 25], [25, 50], [50, 75], [75, 100], [100, None]]}},\n   124\t             'relations': [], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': []}\n   125\tR2_PASSAGES = store_passages('old-2', ['e2620', 'e2889', 'e1732'])\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\tdef r2():\n   129\t    eic = 'equity investment commitments'\n   130\t    return {'figures': [\n   131\t        src('bal', 'e2620', '$25 billion', 25.0, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'as of 2026-07-26')),\n   132\t        src('add18', 'e2889', '$18 billion', 18.0, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'rest of FY2027')),\n   133\t        est('mtk', 3.5, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'rest of FY2027'), 'the MediaTek investment announced after the balance date'),\n   134\t        est('talks', 6.5, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'rest of FY2027'), 'the Anthropic and Thinking Machines talks, risk-adjusted (amount inferred from the stated $53B total)'),\n   135\t        src('ref70', 'e1732', '$70 billion', 70.0, 'USD bn', 'third_party', W('NVIDIA', 'equity investments to ecosystem partners', CO, 'period not specified')),\n   136\t        comp('end', 'roll_forward', ['bal', 'add18', 'mtk', 'talks'], 53.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'end of FY2027'),\n   137\t             relation='overlap_unknown', disputed='add18'),\n   138\t    ], 'answers': [ans('v29', 'end', 3, {'figure': 'ref70'})]}                     # as stored: Bank of America's $70B\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\t# ---------- R3: old-2 call 8595 (v6, four hyperscalers' 2027 data-center capex) ----------\n   142\tFOUR = 'four largest AI hyperscalers'\n   143\tR3_FAMILY = {'members': {'v6': {'what': W(FOUR, 'data-center capex', 'combined', 'CY2027'),\n   144\t                                'bands': [[None, 800], [800, 900], [900, 1100], [1100, 1200], [1200, None]]}},\n   145\t             'relations': [], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': []}\n   146\tR3_PASSAGES = store_passages('old-2', ['e1786', 'e2535', 'e1926'])\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\tdef r3(variant):\n   150\t    if variant == 'a':                                    # the qualifiers stripped, as the stored arithmetic used them\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D725|D729|D730' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -12; nl -ba paid_rehearsal.py | sed -n '17,120p;269,309p;434,447p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D725|D729|D730' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -12; nl -ba paid_rehearsal.py | sed -n '17,120p;269,309p;434,447p'\"","aggregated_output":"10957:## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n10993:- **The questions** (after D725):\n11001:  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n11055:## D729 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate passes (council round 46ad); the paid gate needs its harness built at $0 and Alex's ceiling\n11067:- **Not shown:** how a model uses the format (the paid gate, D725), production lifecycle, the product request builder.\n11073:## D730 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: build the paid gate's harness at $0, then ask for the ceiling\n11075:- **The question** (after D729): \"要不要现在接着搭花钱测试用的发送程序和盲审材料？搭的过程不花钱，搭好、演练、过 council 之后再问你上限（预计 36 次调用，0.2–0.4 美元）。\"\n11080:- **Decided (Alex):** the sender and the blind reading packets for D725's paid gate are built, rehearsed at $0 and reviewed by the\n    17\t\n    18\tPLAN = json.loads((HERE / 'paid-plan.json').read_text())\n    19\tBY_USER = {it['user']: it for it in PLAN}\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\tclass FakeResponse:\n    24\t    def __init__(self, body):\n    25\t        self.body, self.status = body, 200\n    26\t\n    27\t    def read(self):\n    28\t        return self.body\n    29\t\n    30\t    def __enter__(self):\n    31\t        return self\n    32\t\n    33\t    def __exit__(self, *exc):\n    34\t        return False\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\tdef mid(band):\n    38\t    lo, hi = band\n    39\t    return (lo + hi) / 2 if lo is not None and hi is not None else (lo + 10 if lo is not None else hi - 10)\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef valid_answer(it, flavour='ok'):\n    43\t    \"\"\"A schema-valid v13 answer that passes every check: one estimate outcome per member, inside its second rung (a part below its\n    44\t    whole), the reference unavailable. Flavours: 'bad-rung'; 'q3-agree' / 'q3-disagree' (each outcome rests on a company Q3 forecast;\n    45\t    'q3-disagree' gives the Data Center member a different one); 'div-zero' (a ratio over a zero figure).\"\"\"\n    46\t    fprops = it['schema']['properties']['figures']['items']['properties']\n    47\t    aprops = it['schema']['properties']['answers']['items']['properties']\n    48\t    figures, answers = [], []\n    49\t    shared = (it['family'].get('shared') or [None])[0]\n    50\t    for n, view_id in enumerate(it['members']):\n    51\t        m = it['family']['members'][view_id]\n    52\t        band = m['bands'][1]\n    53\t        value = mid(band) - (5.0 * n)\n    54\t        rests = []\n    55\t        if flavour in ('q3-agree', 'q3-disagree', 'q3-float') and shared:\n    56\t            q3 = {k: None for k in fprops}\n    57\t            q3_value = 115.0 if (flavour == 'q3-disagree' and m['what']['scope'] == 'Data Center') else 110.0\n    58\t            if flavour == 'q3-float' and m['what']['scope'] == 'Data Center':\n    59\t                q3_value = 110.00000000000001            # [47b.1] equal within floating-point error, not bit for bit\n    60\t            q3.update(id=f'q3_{view_id}', what=shared, basis='forecast', scenario='base', kind='estimate', value=q3_value, unit='USD bn',\n    61\t                      basis_text='rehearsal Q3', rests_on=[])\n    62\t            figures.append(q3)\n    63\t            rests = [q3['id']]\n    64\t        if flavour == 'div-zero':\n    65\t            z = {k: None for k in fprops}\n    66\t            z.update(id='zero', what=m['what'], basis='forecast', scenario='base', kind='estimate', value=0.0, unit='USD bn', basis_text='zero', rests_on=[])\n    67\t            r = {k: None for k in fprops}\n    68\t            r.update(id='ratio', what=m['what'], basis='forecast', scenario='base', kind='computed', value=1.0, unit='x', operation='ratio', inputs=['zero', 'zero'])\n    69\t            figures += [z, r]\n    70\t        if flavour == 'dc-q4-dup' and m['what']['scope'] == 'Data Center':   # [47c.1] two equal forecasts of one quarter in one answer\n    71\t            for copy in ('a', 'b'):\n    72\t                d = {k: None for k in fprops}\n    73\t                d.update(id=f'dcq4_{copy}', what=dict(m['what'], period='FY2027 Q4'), basis='forecast', scenario='base', kind='estimate',\n    74\t                         value=50.0, unit='USD bn', basis_text='rehearsal DC Q4', rests_on=[])\n    75\t                figures.append(d)\n    76\t            rests = rests + ['dcq4_a', 'dcq4_b']\n    77\t        if flavour in ('q3-dup-total', 'q3-dup-dc') and shared:\n    78\t            if (m['what']['scope'] == 'Data Center') == (flavour == 'q3-dup-total'):\n    79\t                q3 = {k: None for k in fprops}\n    80\t                q3.update(id=f'q3_one_{view_id}', what=shared, basis='forecast', scenario='base', kind='estimate', value=110.0, unit='USD bn',\n    81\t                          basis_text='rehearsal Q3', rests_on=[])\n    82\t                figures.append(q3)\n    83\t                rests = [q3['id']]\n    84\t            else:\n    85\t                for copy in ('a', 'b'):\n    86\t                    q3 = {k: None for k in fprops}\n    87\t                    q3.update(id=f'q3_two_{copy}', what=shared, basis='forecast', scenario='base', kind='estimate', value=110.0,\n    88\t                              unit='USD bn', basis_text='rehearsal Q3', rests_on=[])\n    89\t                    figures.append(q3)\n    90\t        if flavour == 'abstain':\n    91\t            ans = {k: None for k in aprops}\n    92\t            ans.update(view_id=view_id, shape='unresolved', why='the shown passages give no figure for this quantity', reasons='rehearsal',\n    93\t                       cites=[], pushes=[], theme_pushes=[], outcome=None, rung=None, reference=None)\n    94\t            answers.append(ans)\n    95\t            continue\n    96\t        fig = {k: None for k in fprops}\n    97\t        fig.update(id=f'o_{view_id}', what=m['what'], basis='forecast', scenario='base', kind='estimate', value=value, unit='USD bn',\n    98\t                   basis_text='rehearsal estimate', rests_on=rests)\n    99\t        figures.append(fig)\n   100\t        ans = {k: None for k in aprops}\n   101\t        ans.update(view_id=view_id, shape='forecast', outcome=fig['id'], rung=99 if flavour == 'bad-rung' else 2,\n   102\t                   reference={'figure': None, 'unavailable': 'no market figure in the shown passages'}, reasons='rehearsal', cites=[],\n   103\t                   pushes=[], theme_pushes=[])\n   104\t        answers.append(ans)\n   105\t    if flavour == 'q3-agree' and len(it['members']) == 2:   # one shared node in a joint answer\n   106\t        figures = [f for f in figures if f['id'] != f'q3_{it[\"members\"][1]}']\n   107\t        figures[-1]['rests_on'] = [f'q3_{it[\"members\"][0]}']\n   108\t    return {'figures': figures, 'answers': answers}\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef http_error(url, code):\n   112\t    return urllib.error.HTTPError(url, code, f'HTTP {code}', {}, io.BytesIO(json.dumps({'error': {'code': code}}).encode()))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\tclass Stub:\n   116\t    def __init__(self, cfg, scenario, ledger):\n   117\t        self.cfg, self.scenario, self.ledger, self.calls, self.problems, self.sent = cfg, scenario, ledger, {}, [], 0\n   118\t\n   119\t    def expected(self, it, user):\n   120\t        s = self.cfg.rejudging\n   269\t            if defect_arm and k['arm'] == defect_arm and not defect_done:\n   270\t                rd[pid]['K1'] = card(usable, gap='yes')\n   271\t                defect_done = True\n   272\t        first = sorted(rd)[0]\n   273\t        if drop_packet:\n   274\t            rd.pop(first)\n   275\t        if bad_card:\n   276\t            rd[first]['v999'] = rd[first].pop(sorted(rd[first])[0])\n   277\t        if missing_ground:\n   278\t            rd[first][sorted(rd[first])[0]] = card(drop='usable')\n   279\t        if disagree is not None:\n   280\t            rd[first][sorted(rd[first])[0]] = card(b_differs='usable', third=disagree)\n   281\t        if null_ground:\n   282\t            rd[first][sorted(rd[first])[0]]['A']['usable'] = {'answer': 'yes', 'ground': None}\n   283\t        if foreign_ground:\n   284\t            rd[first][sorted(rd[first])[0]]['A']['usable'] = {'answer': 'yes', 'ground': 'the passage about the total'}\n   285\t        return rd\n   286\t\n   287\t    def verdict_of(rd, name, out=None, keys=None, packets_sha=None):\n   288\t        path = scratch / f'readings-{name}.json'\n   289\t        path.write_text(json.dumps({'packets_sha256': packets_sha or clean_sha, 'packets': rd}))\n   290\t        return pg.verdict(out or scratch / 'clean', str(path), keys or keydir)\n   291\t    v = verdict_of(readings(9), 'all-good')\n   292\t    check('verdict: both arms usable everywhere: STOP (gain under 3)', v['verdict'] == 'STOP' and v['joint usable pairs'] == 9 and v['separate usable pairs'] == 9)\n   293\t    v = verdict_of(readings(5), 'gain-4')\n   294\t    check('verdict: joint 9, separate 5: PASS', v['verdict'] == 'PASS', str(v['separate usable pairs']))\n   295\t    v = verdict_of(readings(5, defect_arm='single'), 'single-defect')\n   296\t    check('verdict: one published singleton defect: STOP', v['verdict'] == 'STOP' and len(v['published defects']) == 1)\n   297\t    v = verdict_of(readings(5, defect_arm='separate'), 'separate-defect')\n   298\t    check('verdict: a defect in the separate arm alone does not stop', v['verdict'] == 'PASS')\n   299\t    for name, kw in (('missing packet', {'drop_packet': True}), ('invented card', {'bad_card': True}), ('missing ground', {'missing_ground': True}),\n   300\t                     ('disagreement, no third', {'disagree': None, 'drop_packet': False})):\n   301\t        rd = readings(5, **kw) if name != 'disagreement, no third' else readings(5, disagree={})\n   302\t        v = verdict_of(rd, name.replace(' ', '-').replace(',', ''))\n   303\t        check(f'verdict: {name}: INCOMPLETE', v['verdict'] == 'INCOMPLETE', '; '.join(v['problems'][:1]))\n   304\t    v = verdict_of(readings(5, disagree={'usable': yes('yes')}), 'third-decides')\n   305\t    check('verdict: a disagreement decided by the third reader is complete', v['complete'], '; '.join(v['problems'][:1]))\n   306\t    for name, kw in (('null ground', {'null_ground': True}), ('ground naming nothing in the packet', {'foreign_ground': True})):\n   307\t        v = verdict_of(readings(5, **kw), name.replace(' ', '-'))\n   308\t        check(f'verdict: {name}: INCOMPLETE', v['verdict'] == 'INCOMPLETE', '; '.join(v['problems'][:1]))\n   309\t    v = verdict_of(readings(5), 'other-packets', packets_sha='0' * 64)\n   434\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'abstain')\n   435\t    akeys = scratch / 'key-abstain'\n   436\t    pg.packets(scratch / 'abstain', akeys)\n   437\t    afrozen = json.loads((akeys / 'packet-key.json').read_text())\n   438\t    arend = pg.render_packets(scratch / 'abstain', afrozen)[1]\n   439\t    apid = next(p for p, k in arend.items() if k['unit'] == 'single-S' and k['draw'] == '1')\n   440\t    rd = {pid: {c: card() for c in k['cards']} for pid, k in arend.items()}\n   441\t    for pid, k in arend.items():                            # every draw of single-S abstains\n   442\t        if k['unit'] == 'single-S':\n   443\t            rd[pid] = {'K1': {x: {q: {'answer': 'no', 'ground': 'K1 is unresolved: no figure in the shown passages'} for q in pg.QUESTIONS} for x in ('A', 'B')}}\n   444\t    v = verdict_of(rd, 'abstain', out=scratch / 'abstain', keys=akeys, packets_sha=pg.hashlib.sha256((scratch / 'abstain' / 'packets.md').read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n   445\t    check('abstain: an unresolved singleton is published and can be read with its card as the ground', s['finals']['single-S|single|1']['decision'] == 'publish'\n   446\t          and arend[apid]['grounds'] == ['K1'] and v['complete'], '; '.join(v['problems'][:1]))\n   447\t    # [47c.2, 47d.1] the key orders the packets, and the readers' text commits to it: a swap of two packets whose text is identical\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
