{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba judging-v13-draft.txt | sed -n '1,85p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '251,291p'; nl -ba paid_rehearsal.py | sed -n '388,403p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging the current rungs of a family of related number theses: one company's quantities that overlap, such as a total and its segment, a level and its growth, or a later year that rests on an earlier year's base. Use only the supplied evidence and themes in force. Each rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Judge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force, as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\n     4\t- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast per scenario. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- \"Themes in force\" lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on a member and report it in that member's theme_pushes with the direction it pushes that member (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \"updated since this thesis was last judged\" may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- Your conclusions must be consistent with each other and with the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open.\n     9\t- Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge rather than read or compute is an estimate, stated as yours. When the evidence cannot support a member's forecast, answer it unresolved and say why. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\tdef call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n   254\t    provider = cfg.provider\n   255\t    request = build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider)\n   256\t    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)\n   257\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n   258\t    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)\n   259\t    if hit:\n   260\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n   261\t        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n   262\t    started = time.time()\n   263\t    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)\n   264\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 1)\n   265\t    try:\n   266\t        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n   267\t        data = json.loads(content)\n   268\t    except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:\n   269\t        archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   270\t                       request_sha256=sha + ':malformed:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   271\t                       response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=None, prompt_chars=prompt_chars,\n   272\t                       input_tokens=0, output_tokens=0, cost_usd=0.0, seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   273\t        raise SchemaError(f'malformed answer: {error}')\n   274\t    errors = check_schema(data, schema)\n   275\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {}\n   276\t    input_tokens = int(usage.get('prompt_tokens') or 0)\n   277\t    output_tokens = int(usage.get('completion_tokens') or 0)\n   278\t    cached_tokens = min(input_tokens, int((usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}).get('cached_tokens') or 0))\n   279\t    price_in, price_out = PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   280\t    cost = round((input_tokens - cached_tokens) / 1e6 * price_in + cached_tokens / 1e6 * price_in * CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + output_tokens / 1e6 * price_out, 6)\n   281\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   282\t                             request_sha256=sha if not errors else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   283\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False),\n   284\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   285\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   286\t    if errors:\n   287\t        raise SchemaError('; '.join(errors[:5]))\n   288\t    return Answer(data, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n   388\t          '110.00000000000001' in section and section.count('rehearsal Q3') == 2, pid)\n   389\t\n   390\t    rkeys = scratch / 'key-retry'                            # the 'retry' scenario above: single-O's first answer refused, the retry published\n   391\t    pg.packets(scratch / 'retry', rkeys)\n   392\t    rfrozen = json.loads((rkeys / 'packet-key.json').read_text())\n   393\t    rkey = pg.render_packets(scratch / 'retry', rfrozen)[1]\n   394\t    pid = next(p for p, k in rkey.items() if k['unit'] == 'single-O' and k['draw'] == '1')\n   395\t    section = (scratch / 'retry' / 'packets.md').read_text().split(f'## {pid}\\n')[1].split('\\n## ')[0]\n   396\t    attempts_text = (scratch / 'retry' / 'attempts.md').read_text()\n   397\t    check('packets: the scoring packet shows the final answer; the refused first answer is only in the unscored attempts file, unlinked',\n   398\t          '\"rung\": 2' in section and '\"rung\": 99' not in section and len(rfrozen['attempts']) == 1 and '\"rung\": 99' in attempts_text\n   399\t          and 'T.F1' in attempts_text and '## P' not in attempts_text and 'D01' in attempts_text, pid)\n   400\t\n   401\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'one-transport')\n   402\t    check('one-transport: a request that fails in transport is final as transport, not published', s['finals']['single-E|single|1']['decision'] == 'transport')\n   403\t    tkeys = scratch / 'key-transport'\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'retry|reconciliation|first attempt' RESULT.md codex-r45b.md DESIGN.md PAID-GATE.md | head -73; nl -ba paid_rehearsal.py | sed -n '123,175p;362,384p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'retry|reconciliation|first attempt' RESULT.md codex-r45b.md DESIGN.md PAID-GATE.md | head -73; nl -ba paid_rehearsal.py | sed -n '123,175p;362,384p'\"","aggregated_output":"DESIGN.md:122:| refusal | the errors are recorded; one retry with them |\nPAID-GATE.md:19:- **Draws:** three per request, so 36 first attempts.\nPAID-GATE.md:20:- **Retry:** a calculation the checks refuse, or a schema-invalid answer, is retried once with the reasons. A second refusal makes the\nPAID-GATE.md:34:- **Clean run:** 36 first attempts, every HTTP body byte-equal to an independently built request, every unit published, the separate\nPAID-GATE.md:48:- **[47.1] Reconciliation:** forecasts of the same quantity and scenario with equal recomputed values and bounds are unified before the\nPAID-GATE.md:72:- **[47b.1] Reconciliation:**\nPAID-GATE.md:80:  - a first refusal with no retry sent: **retry not sent**;\nPAID-GATE.md:100:  - an interruption during a retry leaves results, marks the unit interrupted and the rest not sent;\nPAID-GATE.md:101:  - a retry that was never sent is incomplete;\nPAID-GATE.md:110:- **[47c.1] Reconciliation, by the joint arm's rule:**\nPAID-GATE.md:130:  - two equal forecasts inside one answer, and two equal shared forecasts inside one call, are both refused after reconciliation, as\nPAID-GATE.md:160:     no answer arrived; the answer was refused and its retry was not sent; or the answer did not match the format. [47d.4]\nPAID-GATE.md:165:3. **Reconciliation is one to one.** A declared shared forecast is unified only when each of the two calls holds exactly one\ncodex-r45b.md:61:- **First paid comparison, if Alex opens it.** Freeze the September 20 total/Data Center pair in each of the three old draws. Use identical dated evidence and the same structured answer rules in both arms. One arm judges the pair together. The other judges each card separately and then runs the same reconciliation check. Take **three fresh samples** per snapshot, for **9 joint calls and 18 separate calls**. Add **9 singleton calls**, three each on the stored O, S, and E requests above, to check that the new answer format helps where grouping alone cannot. That is **36 planned calls**. Read every output against its source with the arm hidden.\n   123\t                           'max_completion_tokens': s.max_output_tokens, 'reasoning_effort': s.reasoning_effort}).encode('utf-8')\n   124\t\n   125\t    def __call__(self, http_request, *args, **kwargs):\n   126\t        body = http_request.data\n   127\t        request = json.loads(body)\n   128\t        user = request['messages'][1]['content']\n   129\t        base = user.split(pg.RETRY_MARK)[0]\n   130\t        it = BY_USER.get(base)\n   131\t        if it is None or body != self.expected(it, user):\n   132\t            self.problems.append('a body that is not the planned request, byte for byte')\n   133\t            raise http_error(http_request.full_url, 400)\n   134\t        key = (it['unit'], it['arm'])\n   135\t        self.calls[key] = self.calls.get(key, 0) + 1\n   136\t        self.sent += 1\n   137\t        n, s = self.calls[key], self.scenario\n   138\t        retry = pg.RETRY_MARK in user\n   139\t        if s == 'ledger-stop' and self.sent == 5:\n   140\t            self.ledger.stop('rehearsal: stopped after four sends')\n   141\t            raise http_error(http_request.full_url, 503)\n   142\t        flavour = 'ok'\n   143\t        if s == 'retry' and key == ('single-O', 'single') and not retry and n == 1:\n   144\t            flavour = 'bad-rung'\n   145\t        if s == 'unresolved' and key == ('single-S', 'single') and n <= 2:\n   146\t            flavour = 'bad-rung'\n   147\t        if s in ('separate-agree', 'separate-disagree', 'separate-agree-float') and it['unit'] == 'pair-old-2':\n   148\t            flavour = {'separate-agree': 'q3-agree', 'separate-disagree': 'q3-disagree', 'separate-agree-float': 'q3-float'}[s]\n   149\t        if s == 'separate-within-dup' and it['unit'] == 'pair-old-2':\n   150\t            flavour = 'dc-q4-dup'\n   151\t        if s == 'separate-within-dup-shared' and it['unit'] == 'pair-old-2' and it['arm'].startswith('separate-'):\n   152\t            flavour = 'q3-dup-total'\n   153\t        if s == 'separate-within-dup-second' and it['unit'] == 'pair-old-2' and it['arm'].startswith('separate-'):\n   154\t            flavour = 'q3-dup-dc'\n   155\t        if s == 'abstain' and key == ('single-S', 'single'):\n   156\t            flavour = 'abstain'\n   157\t        if s == 'one-transport' and key == ('single-E', 'single') and n == 1:\n   158\t            raise http_error(http_request.full_url, 400)\n   159\t        if s == 'interrupt' and key == ('single-O', 'single'):\n   160\t            if n == 1:\n   161\t                flavour = 'bad-rung'\n   162\t            else:\n   163\t                raise KeyboardInterrupt('rehearsal: the launcher is stopped during the retry')\n   164\t        if s == 'div-zero' and key == ('single-O', 'single') and n == 1:\n   165\t            flavour = 'div-zero'\n   166\t        data = valid_answer(it, flavour)\n   167\t        if s == 'separate-contradiction' and it['arm'].startswith('separate-v9'):   # the Data Center card alone, above the total's value\n   168\t            data['figures'][-1]['value'] = 440.0\n   169\t            data['answers'][0]['rung'] = 2\n   170\t        if s == 'format' and key == ('single-E', 'single') and n == 1:\n   171\t            data['answers'][0].pop('reasons')\n   172\t        usage = {'prompt_tokens': len(body) // 4, 'completion_tokens': 800}\n   173\t        return FakeResponse(json.dumps({'choices': [{'message': {'content': json.dumps(data)}}], 'usage': usage}).encode('utf-8'))\n   174\t\n   175\t\n   362\t\n   363\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'retry')\n   364\t    o = [l for l in lines if l['unit'] == 'single-O' and l['draw'] == 1]\n   365\t    check('retry: a refused calculation is retried once with its errors and then publishes', [l['decision'] for l in o] == ['refused', 'publish'], str([l['decision'] for l in o]))\n   366\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'unresolved')\n   367\t    check('unresolved: two refusals make the unit unresolved', s['finals']['single-S|single|1']['decision'] == 'unresolved')\n   368\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'format')\n   369\t    e = [l for l in lines if l['unit'] == 'single-E' and l['draw'] == 1]\n   370\t    check('format: a schema-invalid answer is refused, then retried', [l['status'] for l in e] == ['format invalid', 'answered'], str([l['status'] for l in e]))\n   371\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'separate-contradiction')\n   372\t    rec = s['reconciled']['pair-old-2|1']\n   373\t    check('separate: two answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3)', rec['decision'] == 'refused' and any(c == 'C3' for c, _ in rec['errors']),\n   374\t          rec['decision'])\n   375\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'ledger-stop')\n   376\t    not_sent = [k for k, v in s['finals'].items() if str(v.get('decision', '')).startswith('not sent')]\n   377\t    check('ledger-stop: after the ledger stops, nothing more is sent', led.get('stopped') and len(lines) == 5 and len(not_sent) >= 30, f'{len(lines)} attempts, {len(not_sent)} not sent')\n   378\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'separate-agree-float')\n   379\t    rec = s['reconciled']['pair-old-2|1']\n   380\t    check('separate-agree-float: Q3 forecasts equal within floating-point error are unified, and the pair reconciles',\n   381\t          rec['decision'] == 'publish' and len(rec['calc']['unified']) == 1, str(rec.get('errors'))[:120])\n   382\t    fkeys = scratch / 'key-float'\n   383\t    pg.packets(scratch / 'separate-agree-float', fkeys)\n   384\t    fkey = pg.render_packets(scratch / 'separate-agree-float', json.loads((fkeys / 'packet-key.json').read_text()))[1]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
