ruediv__(self, name): return Mem(self.s + '\\\\''/'\\\\'' + name)\n    def read_text(self, **kw): return files[self.s]\n    def exists(self): return self.s in files\nit = plan['\\\\''single-E'\\\\'','\\\\''single'\\\\'']\nname = '\\\\''single-E|single|1'\\\\''\nbase = dict(unit='\\\\''single-E'\\\\'', arm='\\\\''single'\\\\'', draw=1)\nrecords = [dict(base, attempt=1, status='\\\\''started'\\\\''), dict(base, attempt=1, status='\\\\''format invalid'\\\\'', decision='\\\\''refused'\\\\'', raw='\\\\''distinct-text-from-returned-model-answer'\\\\''), dict(base, attempt=2, status='\\\\''started'\\\\''), dict(base, attempt=2, status='\\\\''answered'\\\\'', decision='\\\\''publish'\\\\'', data=r.valid_answer(it))]\nfiles = {'\\\\''out/answers.jsonl'\\\\'':'\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\''.join(json.dumps(x) for x in records), '\\\\''out/plan.json'\\\\'':json.dumps([it])}\nout = Mem('\\\\''out'\\\\'')\nresults = {'\\\\''finals'\\\\'':p.derive_finals(out, [it]), '\\\\''reconciled'\\\\'':{}}\nfiles['\\\\''out/results.json'\\\\''] = json.dumps(results)\nprint('\\\\''invalid earlier response in diagnostic file:'\\\\'')\nprint(p.render_attempts(out, [('\\\\''D01'\\\\'',('\\\\''single-E'\\\\'','\\\\''single'\\\\'','\\\\''1'\\\\'',it['\\\\''members'\\\\''][0],1))]))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"separate v14 publish []\nseparate v9 publish []\nfamily check on the same conflicting numbers: refused [('C3', 'FY2027 base: v9 v9.o_v9 (440.0, True, 440.0, True) exceeds v14 v14.o_v14 (425.0, True, 425.0, True)')]\njoint decisions: ['refused', 'publish'] scored: publish\nseparate reconciliation scored: refused\ninvalid earlier response in diagnostic file:\n## D01: What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028?\n  The answer did not match the required format.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY**\n\n1. **The joint side gets a second chance after a conflict that ends the separate side’s run.** In a $0 replay of the old-2 pair, both separate answers passed alone, then failed reconciliation when Data Center revenue was $440B against company revenue of $425B. The same numbers failed the joint check, but a corrected retry counted as published. Score the first attempt on both sides and keep retries for diagnosis. D725’s pass and stop lines can stay as written. [paid_gate.py:181](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:181) · [paid_gate.py:249](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:249) · [RESULT.md:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:86)\n\n2. **Reconciliation can erase a real disagreement about the shared forecast.** On the pinned old-2 plan, I gave the two calls Q3 forecasts of `110 USD bn` and `110 USD`. Both passed alone. The merge discarded the second and published the pair. With both figures preserved, the family check refused it. Require matching units as well as matching values and bounds before unifying figures. [paid_gate.py:266](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:266) · [paid_gate.py:308](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:308)\n\n3. **A returned answer can disappear from blind review.** When the model returns an answer that fails the format check, the journal keeps a raw preview, but the results projection drops it. I replayed that path and the diagnostic file showed only “The answer did not match the required format.” D725 calls for reading every output against its source. Keep that neutral label in the scoring packet and make the returned text and its sources available under an unscored blind label, including when the final attempt fails format. [paid_gate.py:169](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:169) · [paid_gate.py:236](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:236) · [paid_gate.py:542](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:542) · [RESULT.md:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:88)\n\n4. **The packet mapping is fixed, but the readings can still be replaced after scoring.** The rehearsal gets both `STOP` and `PASS` from the same frozen run and packets by supplying different readings files. The verdict only prints its result, so the first completed verdict leaves no binding record. Seal the independent readings and any adjudication before scoring, then write one verdict tied to those exact files. Replaying it should reproduce the recorded verdict. [PAID-GATE.md:195](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:195) · [paid_rehearsal.py:287](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_rehearsal.py:287) · [paid_gate.py:655](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:655)"}}
